TUIOS (Terminal UI Operating System) is a terminal multiplexer and
window manager written in Go. It provides a vim-like modal interface
with multiple terminal panes, workspaces, BSP tiling, kitty graphics
protocol support, and a command palette, all inside your existing
terminal.

A daemon keeps sessions alive, lets you reach sessions on other
machines, and lets coding agents running in your panes report their
state and message each other.
